# stdout is a unit variable (`var`): storage the program keeps, never moved out of. A
# `nom self` method such as close() would take it, so closing descriptor 1 out from under
# the rest of the program is refused while compiling rather than at run time (the ruling
# on #546 moved the handles from `const` to `var`; the refusal moved from CE2400 to CE2436).
# EXPECT_ERROR_CODE: CE2436
use <io/fs>

fn main() i32:
    stdout.close()
    return Result.Ok(0)
